Add predicted difference to last original value.

5. Choosing d
Depends on stationarity.

Use ADF test:

python
Copy
Edit
from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import adfuller
result = adfuller(data)
print('ADF Statistic:', result[0])
print('p-value:', result[1])
If p-value < 0.05 → Stationary → d=0

Else → increase d until stationary.

6. ARIMA vs SARIMA
ARIMA → handles trend.

SARIMA → handles trend + seasonality.

SARIMA adds seasonal parameters (P, D, Q, m).

7. Auto-Selection with pmdarima
python
Copy
Edit
from pmdarima import auto_arima
model = auto_arima(data, seasonal=False, trace=True)
print(model.summary())
Automatically tests combinations of p, d, q.

✅ Key Takeaways:

p → past values

d → remove trend

q → past forecast errors

ARIMA works only if data is stationary → choose d based on ADF/KPSS tests.

Use SARIMA if seasonality exists.